<title>USA: NY Fed's McDonough sees EMU on track for '99 start.</title>
<headline>NY Fed's McDonough sees EMU on track for '99 start.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Federal Reserve Bank President William McDonough said European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) will most likely take off as planned in 1999.</p>
<p>Speaking to the Spanish Institute here McDonough said, &quot;It is highly likely that the Maastricht Treaty will come into effect&quot; as planned.  </p>
<p>McDonough cited the political will among European leaders to make EMU work as a key reason behind his thinking.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it is a political judgment,&quot; McDonough said. &quot;The Maastricht Treaty is a political treaty.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Chris Stetkiewicz, 212-859-1664</p>
</text>
